------------------------------------------------------------------------------
                              Gfile-Checker v1.1

                                   Written by

                       Louis D'ambrosio (aka. Silent One)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Why:

  The Gfile-Checker was written by me as a fast and easy way to announce to
my users that there has been a new gfile added to my system.  Before I was 
announcing new files via news and I wanted something automatic.

How it works:

  The program checks the gfiles: directory by default and examines the "_items2"
file date to see if it is a later time then the users last call time.  You can
also add multiple gfile directories to be checked. It will will take the latest
date of the filelist and go off of that.  Be aware however that if you 
remove, modifiy anything in gfiles that it will announce that there are new
gfiles.  This can be fixed by setting the "_items2" file date back to the old
date.

Installation:

1) Move the file "G-Check" to the "pfiles:bbs" directory. 
2) Edit line 308 in BBSTEXT to read:

     \#0pfiles:bbs/g-check\\n1Scan for new messages (Yes, Brouse, [No])?

3) If you wish to add more directories to be checked just edit the G-Check
   file and at the top you will find the gfiles: entry, just add your own
   directories and it will check those also.  

    For Example:

	/* Directories to check */

	dirs=3					/* Set to total number of directories */
	dir.1="gfiles:"				/* Normally set to GFILES:            */
	dir.2="gfiles:Amiga Articles/"		/* Make sure to use full path and     */
	dir.3="gfiles:General Info Files/"	/* put a "/" at then end.             */

4) Reboot your computer.
5) That be it!


